    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Under Celestial Alignments is the 2026 full-length album by UK instrumental duo Nordic Giants, a masked post-rock outfit known for blending cinematic soundscapes with immersive visuals since their 2010 formation. Self-released on March 13, the record strips back their signature style to its essence—primarily lush piano, searing synths, powerful drums, and subtle horns—creating a cosmic, spacious, and interstellar atmosphere that evokes celestial cycles, human fragility, and our place in the universe. Spanning nine tracks like the opener \"Logos\" with its swelling piano-to-crescendo arc, the slow-burning \"Undertow,\" emotive \"Red Falls,\" darker groover \"Reaper,\" and closing \"Seren,\" it flows as a meditative journey of tension, release, and hope, balancing light and shade in neo-classical, ambient post-rock fashion.\n\nCritics hail it as the band's most authentic and pure effort yet, a grower that stirs deep emotions through mental energy and atmospheric purity, without vocals or ego, feeling like a sacred, spellbinding celebration of existence amid cosmic wonder. Though some note the absence of a big vocal moment, its elegant builds, revolving melodies (as in \"Torus\"), and sci-fi edges confirm Nordic Giants' flawless discography, designed for live theatrical enhancement. This independent gem cements their cult status in progressive and math rock circles, promising euphoric live experiences.",
